// Expected verdict from J. Ševčík, "Program Transformations in Weak Memory Models", PhD thesis, University of Edinburgh, 2008; checked here under sMRD.
// Store buffering with each location under its own monitor.
//
// Source: Ševčík, "Program Transformations in Weak Memory Models" (PhD thesis,
//         Edinburgh 2008), Example 2.5, the classic data-race-free program: x under m1, y under m2.
//
// Data-race-free, so sequentially consistent: one thread's first section
// precedes the other's second, so at least one read sees 1, and r1 = r2 = 0 is
// FORBIDDEN. The other three outcomes are allowed. It needs lock order: before
// it, sMRD allowed r1 = r2 = 0.
//
x := 0; y := 0;
{
  lock m1; x := 1; unlock m1;
  lock m2; r1 := y; unlock m2;
} ||| {
  lock m2; y := 1; unlock m2;
  lock m1; r2 := x; unlock m1;
}
%%
forbid (r1 = 0 && r2 = 0) [sMRD]
